cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KinetiDiff in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "KinetiDiff: Docking-Guided Diffusion for De Novo ACVR1 Inhibitor Design in Fibrodysplasia Ossificans Progressiva"
abstract: >
  KinetiDiff is a structure-based framework for de novo kinase inhibitor design
  that integrates a Geometry-Complete Diffusion Model with real-time AutoDock Vina
  gradient guidance. By injecting physics-based docking gradients into the diffusion
  denoising loop, KinetiDiff steers molecule generation toward high-affinity
  conformations for ACVR1 (ALK2), the causative kinase in Fibrodysplasia Ossificans
  Progressiva.
